Looking at the target shape, the dot sits in the bottom row square just left of the corner square. The piece that covers this square (together with the triangular half of the corner square, shown by the dashed diagonal) is the green piece D — a square joined to a right triangle. Placing D there covers the dotted cell, while the other pieces (A, B, C, E) fill the remaining arm of the L and the vertical column.

Therefore, the piece lying on the dot is D.

\boxed{D}
